        "original_id": "066291a7-a982-5b6f-a9f7-080d23616095",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Williams Gunnison\n- Places: Mount Gunnison, Tomichi Dome\n- Places: Mount Crested Butte, Gothic Mountain, Whetstone Mountain, Mount Axtel, Anthracite Range, Round Mountain, Carbon Peak, Beckwith Mountain, Marcellina Mountain\n- Concepts: laccoliths, Gunnison Country\n\nFacts:\n- John Williams Gunnison was born on November 11, 1812, and he was an American military officer and explorer.\n- Mount Gunnison is named in honor of John Williams Gunnison, who explored the area.\n- Tomichi Dome is associated with other laccoliths in the Gunnison Country, including Mount Crested Butte, Gothic Mountain, Whetstone Mountain, Mount Axtel, Anthracite Range, Round Mountain, Carbon Peak, Beckwith Mountain, Marcellina Mountain, and Mount Gunnison.\n- John Williams Gunnison died on October 26, 1853.",
